{"step_index":1552,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T14:47:48Z","input_tokens":2326,"cache_read_tokens":199202,"output_tokens":2395,"content":"# Phase 5 Implementation Report — Test & Polish Everything\n\nPhase 5 (**Test & Polish Everything**) has been completed. A comprehensive automated audit spanning 82 unit, integration, and regression checks was executed across all components. All working features, execution values, navigation controls, animations, teaching substeps, and interactive prediction capabilities remain verified and intact.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Audit Results\n\n| Category | Tests Run | Result | Key Verification Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **Original Maximum Subarray Example** | 4 | **100% PASS** | Input `[-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]` produces output `6`; best continuous subarray identified as `[4, -1, 2, 1]`. |\n| **All Quick Test Input Datasets** | 16 | **100% PASS** | All-Negative (`-1`), All-Positive (`15`), Single Negative (`-7`), and Single Positive (`42`) matched expected answers. |\n| **Step-by-Step Mathematical Accuracy** | 20 | **100% PASS** | All 9 array element additions and 9 record condition checks (`c >= ans`) evaluated to correct arithmetic values. |\n| **Teaching Substeps & Explanation Integrity** | 3 | **100% PASS** | Generated 197 substeps across 48 execution steps with zero `undefined`, `null`, or `[object Object]` string leaks. |\n| **Bidirectional Navigation & State Restoration** | 4 | **100% PASS** | Forward traversal through all 197 substeps and backward traversal back to Step 0, Substep 0 matched identically in reverse order. |\n| **Interactive Prediction System (Phase 4)** | 3 | **100% PASS** | 29 targeted prediction questions generated; answers cached across navigation; Auto Play pauses on prediction checkpoints. |\n| **Speed Modes & Reduced Motion Accessibility** | 5 | **100% PASS** | `1x` (1200ms), `1.5x` (750ms), `2x` (450ms), and `0.5x` (2200ms) with `--anim-speed-factor`; `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` compliant. |\n| **Non-Kadane DSA Compatibility** | 2 | **100% PASS** | Binary Search on `[2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12]` for target `8` found index `3` with full condition and variable tracing. |\n| \n<truncated 2170 bytes>\nut chips, interactive prediction card, loop pointer strip, condition gate, and calculation stage. |\n| [app_build/styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css) | Verified | High-contrast pedagogical theme, CSS variable `--anim-speed-factor`, `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`, `@media (max-width: 768px)` mobile ordering, variable card animations, and prediction choice states. |\n| [app_build/explainer.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js) | Verified | Granular 3-part teaching substeps (`whatIsHappening`, `whyNecessary`, `whatHappensNext`), real-value arithmetic breakdowns, condition evaluation logic, and `buildPredictQuestion()`. |\n| [app_build/app.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js) | Verified | Bidirectional step navigation (`goToPrevSubstep`, `goToNextSubstep`, `goToStep`), Auto Play with prediction checkpoint pauses, speed adjustment, DOM rendering, and answer state caching. |\n| [scratch/test_phase5.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_phase5.js) | Created | Standalone test runner verifying 82 automated test cases without external cloud dependencies. |\n\n---\n\n### Key Verification Highlights\n\n1. **Reversibility**: Moving backward from the final return step step-by-step to step 1 cleanly restores all memory snapshots, active line highlights, condition badges, and variable cards in exact reverse order without throwing exceptions.\n2. **Offline Autonomy**: Operates 100% client-side in standard web browsers using vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No external AI keys, cloud servers, or network requests required.\n3. **Responsive UI**: Single-column vertical layout on mobile devices (`<= 768px`) prioritizes the Teaching Area at the top (`order: 1`), followed by Code (`order: 2`) and Variables (`order: 3`), ensuring learners see explanations without excessive horizontal scrolling.","thinking":"Verifying all existing functionalities; confirm maximum subarray example produces the expected output (6). Conducting a thorough check of variable values, conditional logic, loop iterations, and navigation within the application. Aiming to identify any UI issues or discrepancies in explanations.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
