{"step_index":1580,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T15:08:54Z","input_tokens":2622,"cache_read_tokens":220708,"output_tokens":2050,"thinking":"The large white space in `visualConditionGate` is an anomaly. The `cond-balance-row`, rendered with white background and padding, occupies the space where the comparison `1 >= -2` and execution status (`✓ EXECUTES`, `SKIPPED`) reside. The visual style of `cond-balance-row` indicates this style could be the cause.\n\n\nThe excessive vertical space consumption suggests a layout issue where individual components are vertically stacked without proper containment. Investigating how the `visual-condition-gate` interacts with its children and overall page structure is critical. The large amount of information present at once, even after scrolling, makes the interface feel overwhelming and likely contributes to the user needing to scroll so far to see the entire condition.\n\n\nThe excessive vertical space stems from vertically stacked, uncontained components with large gaps. The `.teaching-card-inner` layout is the primary source of the problem. A deep dive is needed to examine its structure and understand how to reduce the gaps and improve component containment.\n\n\nInvestigating font size and padding as primary causes for excessive space. Reducing font sizes and tightening padding on the pedagogical explanation card and condition gate components is hypothesized to significantly decrease vertical footprint. The goal is to create a more compact and scannable interface. Consolidating the lesson card content into a unified structure, with integrated symbols, can achieve further vertical space reduction.\n\n\nInvestigating the visual design of the components, specifically the Thonny expression evaluator and the calculation box. Reducing the padding and gap of the Thonny box, and eliminating redundancy in the calculation box by conditionally hiding it, are proposed improvements. Examination of the variable box card's padding is underway to determine if it can be further reduced.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css\"","EndLine":"1050","StartLine":"980","toolAction":"\"Viewing var-box-card in styles.css\"","toolSummary":"\"View var-box-card in styles.css\""}}]}
